-- title:
--   The rational ℓ-adic Hecke algebra on J₀(p) is reduced
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $\ell$ be natural numbers, both assumed prime. Write $J =$ `JZero p` for the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $p$ base-changed to an algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\mathbf Q$, i.e. the quotient of the group of degree-zero divisors by the subgroup of principal divisors, the geometric Jacobian of $X_0(p)$ in this presentation. Equip $J$ with the module structure `heckeModuleBar p` over the Hecke polynomial ring $\mathbb T = \mathbf Z[T_q : q \text{ prime}]$, realised as `HeckeAlg` $=$ `MvPolynomial Nat.Primes ℤ`: this is the structure obtained from the ring homomorphism `heckeEvalBar` sending the variables to the geometric Hecke correspondences on $J$ when these pairwise commute, and from the evaluation of all variables at $0$ otherwise. The assertion is that the $\mathbf Q_\ell$-subalgebra `rationalHeckeAlgebra ℓ (JZero p)` of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbf Q_\ell}\bigl(\mathbf Q_\ell \otimes_{\mathbf Z_\ell} T_\ell(J)\bigr)$ generated by the image of the resulting representation $\mathbb T \to \operatorname{End}_{\mathbf Q_\ell}(V_\ell(J))$, obtained by base change from the action of $\mathbb T$ on the $\ell$-adic Tate module $T_\ell(J)$, is a reduced ring: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements.
--
--   This is the reducedness of the rational $\ell$-adic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T'_\ell \subseteq \operatorname{End}_{\mathbf Q_\ell}(V_\ell(J_0(p)))$ acting on the Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_0(p)$, which at prime level reflects the fact that the integral Hecke algebra on weight-two cusp forms is reduced and finite free over $\mathbf Z$. It is used in the analysis of inertia acting on the Tate module, specifically in [`ModularCurve.exists_generator_tateModule_closure_inertia_smul_sub_adjoin_tateHeckeRep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_generator_tateModule_closure_inertia_smul_sub_adjoin_tateHeckeRep) and [`ModularCurve.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_tateModule_rep_ne_of_adjoin_tateHeckeRep_apply_ne_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_tateModule_rep_ne_of_adjoin_tateHeckeRep_apply_ne_zero).
